        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Trijumf',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trijumf (Croatian Triumph) is a popular trick-taking game played along the Croatian coast and islands. It combines elements of Briscola and Tressette using a 40-card Italian deck. Features A-3-K ranking, trump suits, AkuÅ¾anje (declarations for bonus points), and plays to 401 or 501 points.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Trijumf, also known as Croatian Triumph, is a card game popular on the Croatian coast and islands. Although the name is similar to Italian trionfo, the Croatian version is more similar to the Venetian game madrasso, with some elements of marianna.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '2 or 4 (partnerships)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '40 cards (Triestine). Rank: A-3-K-Kt-J-7-6-5-4-2. Values: A=11, 3=10, K=4, Kt=3, J=2. Total 120 + 10 for last trick = 130.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, score sheet',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '10 cards each. Trump determined by card flip or declaration.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
